1.	Calendar year 1936,	$14,502,260.04;
Calendar year 1937, $18,854,202.49; Calendar year 1938, $16,055,880.75.
2 and 3. Statistics are not kept relative to the amount of taxes collected on goods entered under the various tariff items.

The following information furnished by the National Harbours Board:
Amount voted for Churchill harbour in estimates for 1937-38: (a) Capital, $10,000;
(b)	Deficit, $242,000. Work provided under item (a) Carried out; (b) Actual deficit realized $140,889. Difference between latter figure and amount voted represents expenditures not required or deferred in view of restricted operations owing to short crop.
